SLUG: services/vehicle-transport.html
TITLE: Car & Bike Transport in Kanpur — covered carriers
DESC: Cars and two-wheelers moved out of Kanpur in covered carriers rather than driven, with condition photographed at both ends. What papers you need and how it is priced.
HEADING: Car &amp; bike transportation
LEAD: Vehicles travel in a covered carrier rather than being driven across — nothing is added to the odometer and the paint is not exposed to a thousand kilometres of road.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Services|/services.html ; Vehicle transport|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <h2>Carried, not driven</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            The cheapest way to move a car between cities is to pay somebody to
            drive it. It is also the way that adds hundreds of kilometres to the
            odometer, wears the clutch and tyres, and puts your vehicle in
            someone else's hands on a highway.
          </p>
          <p>
            We carry vehicles on a covered carrier instead. The vehicle is
            loaded, chocked and strapped at the wheels — never over the body —
            and travels enclosed. Its condition is recorded and photographed
            before loading and again at delivery, so there is a shared record
            rather than an argument.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-car"/></svg></span>
          <h3>What you need to have ready</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Registration certificate and a valid insurance copy</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Fuel at roughly a quarter tank — enough to load and unload, no more</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Personal belongings removed from the vehicle</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>A spare key available at both ends</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Any existing damage pointed out before loading</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">How it is priced</span>
        <h2>What changes the cost</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Route and distance</h3>
          <p>Carriers run established routes. A vehicle going along one of those costs less than one needing a detour.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Vehicle size</h3>
          <p>A hatchback, an SUV and a motorcycle each take a different amount of space on the carrier.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Door pickup or depot</h3>
          <p>Collection from your door costs more than dropping the vehicle at a loading point, and large carriers often cannot enter residential lanes at all.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow">
        <h2>Questions we get asked</h2>
        <div class="faq mt-6" data-faq>
          <details>
            <summary>Can my car be transported with my household goods?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              It travels on a vehicle carrier, not in the goods truck, but both
              can run on the same booking and be coordinated to arrive around
              the same time. One coordinator handles both.
            </p></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is the vehicle insured during transport?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              Your own motor policy and any transit cover offered are separate
              things. Ask us what cover applies to the carrier and confirm with
              your insurer what your policy covers while the vehicle is being
              transported — do not assume either one covers everything.
            </p></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can you collect from my building?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              Where the lane allows a carrier, yes. Many residential streets do
              not, in which case we agree a nearby loading point. We check this
              at booking rather than discovering it on the day.
            </p></div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How are two-wheelers handled?</summary>
            <div class="faq__body"><p>
              Motorcycles and scooters are crated or secured upright on stands
              and strapped at the frame. Mirrors are usually folded or removed
              to avoid contact in transit.
            </p></div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-tight cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow text-centre">
        <h2>Moving a vehicle?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Tell us the make, both cities, and whether you need door pickup.</p>
        <div class="btn-row mt-6 btn-row--centre">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact.html" data-open-callback>Request a callback</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/services.html">All services</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
